This extension adds God of War (2018) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Auto-updates boot-info.json. Supports Script Loader.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Script Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "version.dll" file and a "loader_config.toml" file.[/*]
[*]Exec folder mods with an "exec" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Patch Folder mods with a "patch" folder install to the "exec" folder.[/*]
[*]Exec subfolder mods with an "ActivityFeed", "cinematics", "dc", "languages", "sound" or "wad" folder install to the "exec" folder.[/*]
[*]Texpack/Lodpack mods with a ".texpack" or ".lodpack" file install to the "exec\patch\pc_le" folder.[/*]
[*]Lua mods with a "lua" folder and a ".lua" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Save (User Home) mods with a ".sav" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\God of War\<User ID>" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Places .texpack and .lodpack mods into the correct folder automatically, based on how the files were packaged by the mod author.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff00]Includes Load Order support, and updates boot-options.json file with any .texpack and .lodpack mods installed.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Automatically installs save games with mod type "Save Games (Documents)" to your Documents folder.[/*]
[*]You can open the boot-options.json file and several other files and folders using the buttons in the Folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][b][color=#f6b26b]You can download the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/godofwar/mods/89]Script Loader[/url]﻿﻿﻿ using the button in the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/color][/b][/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for God of War (2018) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Script Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "version.dll" file and a "loader_config.toml" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

exec folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "exec" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

patch Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "patch" folder.

  Installs to: "exec"

========================================================================

exec subfolder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ActivityFeed", "cinematics", "dc", "languages", "sound" or "wad" folder.

  Installs to: "exec"

========================================================================

Texpack/Lodpack:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".texpack" or ".lodpack" file.

  Installs to: "exec\patch\pc_le"

========================================================================

Lua Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "lua" folder and a ".lua" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".sav" extension.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\God of War\<User ID>"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
